# _Build local runtime artifacts - never commit these.
#
# Every pattern below is listed exactly ONCE. The file previously carried four
# of them twice (logs/, build-reports/, .gbuildcache/, test-results*.xml), split
# across two independently-edited blocks. A duplicate is not harmless: it reads
# as two independent rules, so deleting one looks like it narrows coverage when
# it does not, and a future edit that removes "the" copy leaves the other
# behind with nothing indicating it was ever there.

# --- Tool state -----------------------------------------------------------------
.tools/                 # vendored PSScriptAnalyzer etc.; not in a fresh checkout
.gbuild/                # per-device locale cache (deviceId hash + UI language)
.gbuildcache/           # incremental build cache
.gbuildstate
*.gbuildstate
.gbuild-state.gbuildstate
.gbuild-circuitbreaker.gbuildstate
# Lock files sit beside the state they guard and were previously UNTRACKED:
# .gbuild-state.gbuildstate.lock, .gbuildcache/index.json.lock,
# build-reports/autotune-history.jsonl.lock, logs/*/audit.log.lock. A committed
# lock is not just clutter - it advertises a stale exclusive handle to anyone
# who clones, and `git status` noise hides real changes.
*.lock

# --- Reports and telemetry ------------------------------------------------------
build-reports/
distributed-report/
reports/
*.sdkcache.json
last-run-*.log
suite-progress-*.log
Tests/suite-progress-*.log

# --- Test artifacts -------------------------------------------------------------
test-results*.xml
testResults.xml
TestResults/
Tests/TestResults/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.aider*

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vault key/salt filenames are NOT always suffixed (e.g. logs/test/vault.key),
# so *.vault.key alone leaves them exposed outside logs/.
vault.key
*.vault.key
*.vault.salt
*.salt

# --- Misc -----------------------------------------------------------------------
gbuild-standalone-*/
# Stray files produced by un-escaped cmd.exe redirects in batch fixtures
# (a `>nul`r`n...` redirect creates a file literally named `nul`r`nexit`).
nul*
# logs/ is covered above.
# Build output note: output is written into ProjectRoot, so it is harmless when
# the project is a real checkout - but when gbuild is launched from a directory
# that only CONTAINS projects (a folder of repos) it lands beside that folder
# and is shared by every project underneath it. testResults.xml and
# build-reports/ were both found next to the tool for exactly this reason.
#
# Ad-hoc debug scripts at the tool root (debug-*.ps1) are deliberately NOT
# ignored: they ship with the tree and would escape the -SyntaxCheck scope
# (Modules/Steps/Hooks only), which is how one once carried a real parse error
# plus a backslash path literal that tripped the platformPathLiterals gate.
# Debug against a scratch copy outside the repo instead.

.gbuild/
.gbuildcache/
logs/
publish-output/

# --- added by gsync security gate ---
# === SECURITY ===
ssh_id
*.pfx
.env
bin/
obj/
node_modules/
.vs/
*.apk
*.aab

# --- added by gsync security gate ---
*.p12
*.key
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp
*.log
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
*.orig
*.rej
.cache/
*.env
secrets.*
*.secret
*.pem
.gsync.state
sync-outputs/
# Machine-level signing profile: state of THIS machine, never shipped.
profiles/
